course: dictionary
lesson: 649
title: Many meanings of bad
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word bad has many meanings, so you must use the words around it to find the right one. This is context at work. Ask yourself: what does bad mean in this sentence, and would another meaning fit better?
explain: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can collapse or be full of bad air.» Here bad means harmful. The warning about collapse tells you the air is dangerous, not that it smells nasty.
explain: «Nearly everyone is bad for the first weeks and finds practice boring» means not yet good at something. Bad can mean not skilled, and the phrase for the first weeks hints that it will not last.
explain: Bad can also mean rotten, naughty or sorry. «The milk has gone bad» means spoiled. «I feel bad about it» means sorry. Swap in a meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Bad is an adjective: bad, worse, worst.
fact: «Bad weather» means not good weather, or weather of low quality.
fact: «Smoking is bad for you» means harmful, so it can hurt you.
fact: «The milk has gone bad» means rotten or spoiled.
fact: «Not bad» means quite good, and «bad luck» means unlucky.
exercise: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels; they can collapse or be full of bad air.» What does bad air mean here? | Fresh air from the sea | *Air that is harmful to breathe | Air that smells of flowers | Cold air in winter
exercise: «The milk has gone bad.» What does bad mean here? | *Rotten, spoiled | Naughty | Quite good | Sorry
exercise: Dad says, «That's not the worst idea you've had.» What does he mean? | Dad is angry with you | An idea nobody has had before | A terrible idea | *A good idea, said in a dry way
test: «I feel bad about it.» What does bad mean here? | *Sorry, feeling regret | Ill and in bed | Harmful to your health | Quite good
test: «The bad guy hid in the tower.» What does bad mean here? | Rotten, spoiled | *A villain, a wicked character in a story | Not good at hiding | Very sorry
exam: «There seemed to be no end to this wood, and no beginning, and no difference in it, and, worst of all, no way out.» What does worst mean here? | Brightest of all | *Most terrible of all | Best of all | Quietest of all
